  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Tanmit Singh vs State Of Maharashtra on 22 February, 2023 Author: N.R. Borkar Bench: N.R. Borkar 2023:Bhc-As:14508 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 225 Of 2023 Jaspal Singh ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent With Anticipatory Bail Application No. 226 Of 2023 Tanmit Singh ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent ......... Mr. Subhradeep Banerjee a/w Ms. Megha Chandra a/w Mr. A. R. Sawant for the Applicants. Ms. Rutuja Ambekar, App for the State. ......... Coram : N.R. Borkar, J. Dated : 22 February 2023 P.C. :- . The applicants who are accused in Crime No. 224 of 2022 registered at Wadiwarhe Police Station, Nashik for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 179, 272, 273, 328, 420 r/w 34 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(d), 30(2)(a), 3(1)(zz)(i), 1(zz)(v) and 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 have filed these applications under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure for anticipatory bail.",
    "facts": "3. On 30 December 2022, pursuant to secret information trucks bearing registration No. RJ-06-GB-5203 and RJ-09-GB-0472 were intercepted and on inspections of the said trucks, Gutkha packets (Prohibited Tobacco Products) worth Rs. 1,95,87,000/- were found in the said trucks. According to the prosecution, the present applicants are owners of the said trucks.",
    "arguments": "4. The learned counsel for the applicants submits that the applicants had already sold the trucks in question to third party.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. The learned counsel for the applicants submits that the applicants had already sold the trucks in question to third party.",
